					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-12 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1036/542227121_96d1812d8e.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="304" height="323" /><br /><br />It&#39;s probably the closest they&#39;ll ever get to <strong>Enrique Iglesias</strong>, but they&#39;ll take it. Peep out <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> on the <a href="http://www.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=music&amp;MyToken=8e0b34bc-2a87-4cf5-902a-ae44ff79719c">Myspace Music</a> featured artist page!<br /><br />&quot;Bayani&quot; in stores today!!! <br /><br />Peep the blog all day for updates...<br />daps1<br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-11 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><span class="Apple-style-span">One day left. Unless you&#39;re trying to be the first to cop the album (after the album release party) - <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">TONIGHT at Easy Street Records in Seattle </span>(Queen Anne location)! Sabzi and I will be rocking a live set <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">FREE</span> tonight at <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">11pm</span>. Then, <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">Bayani</span></span> will be put on sale right before midnight to keep in line with the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">JUNE 12</span> release date. It goes down. Then we&#39;ll kick it some more. Then we go to sleep, wake up and bam - BAYANI IN STORES NOW nationwide! </span><div><br /></div><div>BLUE SCHOLARS IN-STORE PERFORMANCE</div><div>BAYANI - Midnight Album Release</div><div>MONDAY, JUNE 11 - 11PM</div><div>Easy Street Records (Queen Anne)</div><div>Seattle, WA</div><div>FREE!!!</div><div><br /></div><div>*************</div><div><br /></div><div>Also, a handful of album reviews:</div><div><br /></div><div><span style="font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><a href="http://www.threeimaginarygirls.com/bluescholars07may">Three Imaginary Girls</a></span></div><div><span style="font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><a href="http://www.pitchforkmedia.com/article/record_review/43224-bayani">Pitchfork</a></span></div><div><span style="font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><a href="http://www.smokingsection.net/TSS/?p=1393">The Smoking Section</a></span></div><div><span style="font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><a href="http://www.allhiphop.com/reviews/?ID=1220">Allhiphop.com</a></span></div><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px"><a href="http://www.urb.com/reviews/cd/feature.php?ReviewId=364">URB</a></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-11 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><span class="Apple-style-span">You catch the benefit concert on Saturday night (6/9) at Chop Suey? No? Well not only did you miss <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Sleep</span> and <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Grayskul</span> kill it with new material. <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">RA</span> and <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Saba</span> debuted some new tracks off the upcoming <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Common Market</span> album tentatively titled <span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Tobacco Road</span></span>. One cut in particular called <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">&quot;Trouble Is&quot;</span> turned more than a few heads. If and when you catch it live, you&#39;ll know what I&#39;m talking about. </span><div><br /></div><div><span class="Apple-style-span">And a belated big up to the <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">2007 Youth Speaks</span> <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Seattle</span> poetry slam team (Dakota, Rose, Khatsini and Ronnie) heading down to San Jose in July to rep at the Brave New Voices festival.</span></div><div><br /></div><div><span class="Apple-style-span">Also, <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">THE MASSLINE STORE IS OPEN</span>! Hurry up and buy!</span></div><div><br /></div><div>Isulong!</div><div>Geo</div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-10 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1385/538877262_191a526f28.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" height="323" /><br /><em>Geo and new Blue Scholar fan Alexander chillin at South Seattle Community College last night. Photo by CGC.<br /><br /></em>Last night, <strong>Blue Scholars</strong>, along with yours truly delivering the cuts, performed at <strong><a href="http://www.lelo.org/" target="_blank">LELO</a></strong>&#39;s annual Domingo, Viernes and Jefferson Awards Dinner at South Seattle Community College. <strong>Lt. Ehren Watada</strong>, also on hand to receive honors, introduced <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> to the packed house. The <em>&quot;Back Home&quot;</em> video was shown right before the guys went through a set of all new material from the <strong>Bayani</strong> album, in stores everywhere on June 12. Shout out to LELO, Ehren, the Watada family, all working class folks and their families, and your mom&#39;s mom!<br /><br /><strong>Blue Scholars</strong>, just fresh off the Massline west coast tour, stay busy <strong>today</strong> with another performance at the Seattle Center. Come check them out and other quality acts (hip hop and non) at the 2007 Pagdiriwang Philippine Festival&#39;s <a href="http://farm2.static.flickr.com/1121/530584105_3a943a41f1_o.jpg">Diwa Na Kalayaan</a> showcase, starting around 1pm. Big up to all the organizers and Battalion Entertainment.<br /><br />See you at the in-stores!<br />Peace<br />dj daps1<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-07 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><strong>Blue Scholars - Back Home</strong><br /><br />directed by Zia Mohajerjasbi<br /><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/En8DwCeKa6M"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/En8DwCeKa6M"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object><br /><div align="justify">Here it is, the first music video for Bayani.  Many humble thanks to director Zia Mohajerjasbi, producers Rahwa Habte, Kirby Grey, Sam Terry, our stellar cast of soufenders, the youth at WAPIFASA, and everybody else who put in hella work to make this project jump off.  Get ready folkers, this is just the beginning.<br /><br />-Saba</div></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> [31] <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=290">[59]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[&gt;&gt;]</A>  </span></p>
